{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/872217-how-do-you-justify-throngs-existing-in-universe","id":872217,"title":"How do you justify throngs existing in-universe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-23T01:40:28-07:00","id":872217,"title":"How do you justify throngs existing in-universe?","content":"First of all, I'm a total newb when it comes to PtC. I'm very interested in running a game based on what I've read here and at the White Wolf wiki, but I'm holding off on reading the actual rulebook until 2E comes out. (This gives me time to finish a CtL Chronicle before I'm too hyped on PtC to continue it! That almost happened when I bought WtF2E...) I've been tossing around my chronicle idea with an interested player, and she seems very against any handwaving related to how a throng might come together: since Created are by necessity rare to keep with the theme of isolation, how have you experienced STs formed your characters' throngs? How do you justify a group of Created--against all odds--managing to come together at the same time and place? Is the best explanation the old handwave &quot;it happened over a long period of time, yet somehow none of us have completed a single milestone?&quot;<br /> <br /> I realize that one alternative is a joint creation, but that seems even weaker in my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8335-pondrthis","name":"pondrthis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T05:00:56-07:00","id":872282,"title":"","content":"Drop the &quot;none of us completed a single Milestone&quot;, and &quot;over time&quot; is completely valid. Make up Milestone imbalances in other ways.<br /> <br /> Also, things like Quashmallim and Elpis visions guiding Prometheans is very much an in-setting thing. Some of the 1E Promethean fiction even has a Quashmal driving one Created out of their &quot;home&quot; seemingly so they can meet up with another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T08:34:12-07:00","id":872391,"title":"","content":"Promethean is a game in which Deus Ex Machinas are a mystery to resolve rather than a weak plot point (if used correctly). My players all met in a library, at night, during a blizzard, because they dreamed of that place for days or even weeks, travelling slowly to find it.<br /> <br /> Was it a huge D.E.M.? Yes. Did my players question it? No, they had faith in the Divine Fire and knew that this was no mere coincidence. One player was fighting against his visions, his pilgrimage stuck in limbo for a long time, and it had created a huge wasteland; once the others learned of the terrible thunderstorm and the &quot;haunted house&quot; nearby, they knew why the Divine Fire had brought them together: to save one of their own from his foolishness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:23:43-07:00","id":872436,"title":"","content":"Prometheans also tend to be able to sense strange pulses of the divine fire, and a flaring of Azoth somewhere for some reason is probably going to bring Prometheans to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:30:20-07:00","id":872443,"title":"","content":"I did a joint creation for my chronicles, and it was intended to be a central mystery and catalyst for the length of the chronicle. It's only as weak as your justification for it. <br /> <br /> The chronicle in the 1e books begin with an alchemist summoning the throng together by means of tripping their Azothic senses. And by means of Azoth (and soon, Azothic Memory), Elpis, and Firestorms, there's quite a few more ways to bring a throng together. Fellow travelers and the player imperative to cooperate should hopefully do the rest.<br /> <br /> And there isn't real need to firmly state things like &quot;never had a milestone&quot;. Just because everyone started in play with the same number of dots doesn't mean that every one began life on equal footing. 2e might make that harder to state definitively, since progress is now hardwired into the splat, but that still remains to be seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T09:32:46-07:00","id":872444,"title":"","content":"There's also nothing saying they have to all have met at the same time. Promethean A meets Promethean B and they're confronted with a problem, they're both a little out of their depth but B remembers meeting Promethean C in passing years ago and still has a way to contact her. C is willing to help but still isn't an expert on what they're dealing with, but she used to be in a throng with Promethean D who is. The rarity of Prometheans also makes the degrees of separation between them smaller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T11:21:55-07:00","id":872535,"title":"","content":"Thanks all, there's some golden advice in there. I should say I (unfairly) discounted the ideas of creation-as-plot and guiding visions because they're too similar to the main points of said Changeling game, with which I'm getting bored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8335-pondrthis","name":"pondrthis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T22:23:01-07:00","id":877355,"title":"","content":"In 2E, is there some sort of gestalt subconsciousness/Akhashic Memory to explain why there is a culture in Promethean despite there being so few of them? Could that also be a thing that draws Prometheans together, subconsciously?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T23:07:52-07:00","id":877383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/872217-how-do-you-justify-throngs-existing-in-universe?p=877355#post877355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2E, is there some sort of gestalt subconsciousness/Akhashic Memory to explain why there is a culture in Promethean despite there being so few of them? Could that also be a thing that draws Prometheans together, subconsciously?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Azothic Memory. It's been mentioned several times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}